WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.830
Take the brief, build the pieces, and quote a job that pays.

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.380
This is the video for module two of Event Decoration and Styling.

3
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:19.490
Most disputes start with words like elegant, or not too much, that mean different things to you and the client. A brief turns those words into written decisions.

4
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:27.350
Ask about the event times and when guests arrive. Ask when you can enter the venue, and when you must clear out.

5
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:41.310
Ask the number of guests and tables. Ask for colours with photos of the aso ebi, three pictures they love, and one they dislike. One disliked picture can save you from a wrong direction.

6
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:54.750
Ask which zones to decorate, the budget for decor only, and the venue's rules. Then send a written summary back, measure the venue, and buy nothing until the client approves in writing.

7
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.320
Inflate 11 inch balloons slightly under full size, so they are rounder and less likely to burst. Use a sizer so they match.

8
00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:10.900
Inflate some 18 inch balloons for volume, and many 5 inch balloons for filling gaps.

9
00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:17.160
Tie two balloons together to make a pair, then twist two pairs into a cluster of four.

10
00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:23.360
Push the knots through a balloon strip, rotating each cluster so the garland is round.

11
00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:37.650
Attach it to the stand with cable ties, then fill gaps with glue dots. Do not guess numbers. Build 30 cm, count, multiply by the length you need, and add about 10 percent for bursts.

12
00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:46.320
Some guests are allergic to latex. For an indoor event with a known allergy, use foil balloons and fabric instead.

13
00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:54.010
Keep foil balloons away from overhead power lines, because the metallic coating can conduct electricity.

14
00:01:55.260 --> 00:02:04.180
And never hang fabric from light fittings, fans or electrical cables. If the hall has no safe fixing points, use free-standing frames.

15
00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:11.740
For example, Grace has 12 round tables, each 60 inches across, and wants floor-length cloths.

16
00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:18.220
A standard table is about 30 inches high, so the drop is 30 inches on each side.

17
00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:25.760
60, plus two times 30, is 120. She needs 120 inch round cloths.

18
00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:37.680
She orders 13, one spare in case of a stain. For backdrops, use about 1.5 to 2 times the frame width in fabric, so it gathers and looks full.

19
00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:48.920
Many decorators work hard and still lose money because they price by feeling. Here is a quote that covers every naira. These prices are rough illustrations.

20
00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:57.990
Materials she uses up, such as balloons and flowers, come to 86,000 naira. Rentals are 39,000.

21
00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:03.830
She adds 10,000 for wear on her own pump and stands, so she can replace them.

22
00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:11.720
Labour for her and 2 helpers, including pack-down, is 50,000. Transport is 20,000.

23
00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:16.210
That is a subtotal of 205,000 naira.

24
00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:25.740
Tolu adds 10 percent contingency for price changes and breakages. That makes 225,500.

25
00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:34.350
Then about 25 percent profit. She rounds her quote to 282,000 naira, with each zone listed.

26
00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:43.040
Never buy or rent for a client without a deposit. Many decorators ask 50 to 70 percent on approval.

27
00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:49.560
Collect the balance a few days before the event, and write your cancellation terms on the quote.

28
00:03:50.810 --> 00:04:04.660
Accept a payment only when it shows in your own bank or wallet app. Screenshots can be faked. And if a client says it is too high, remove a zone or swap fresh flowers for artificial. Do not cut your profit.

29
00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:20.780
To remember. Get the brief and the approval in writing. Test-build your garland and count. Cloth equals table plus two times the drop. Quote every cost plus profit. Take a deposit first, and cut scope, not profit.

30
00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:35.040
Now run a practice brief with a friend and write a one-page proposal. Practise a garland, fabric gathers and a place setting at home. Then price a real job with deposit and cancellation terms.

31
00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:37.330
Continue with the lessons below.
